# Business Certification — End-to-End Scenario Mandate (CO-QA-001)

Status: **ENTERPRISE APPROVED** · Permanent  
**Authority:** **CO-QA-001** — `.cursor/rules/co-qa-001-enterprise-regression-certification.mdc`

This rule provides operational detail for Scenario Packs. Conflict resolution: **CO-QA-001 wins**.

## Constitutional rule (CO-QA-001)

Every Business Certified module must include at least one real end-to-end business scenario. Re-run it whenever a related domain changes. Build / TypeScript / Lint / verify / smoke do **not** grant Business Certification. Scenario Fail ⇒ module remains **OPEN**.

## What “real end-to-end business scenario” means

1. Uses **real business identities** (Contact / Company / Opportunity / Deal / Document / Task as applicable) — not only mock fixtures asserted in Node scripts.  
2. Walks the **canonical business path** for that module (create → work → verify outcome in UI).  
3. Asserts **observable business outcomes** the Product Owner cares about.  
4. Is documented as a reusable **Scenario Pack** for that module.  
5. Is **re-executed** after any change that touches a related domain.

## Related domain change → mandatory re-run

- Persistence mode, purge, storage keys, migrations  
- Association / ownership / identity keys  
- Registry / API list-query filters  
- Hydration / projection adapters  
- Document / task / deal / opportunity linkage  
- Navigation or workspace entry that loads the entity  

## Scenario Pack minimum template

Store under `docs/<sprint-or-module>/` as `*-E2E-SCENARIO.md`:

```markdown
## E2E Business Scenario Pack — <Module>

### Scenario ID
<MODULE>-E2E-001

### Business path
Contact/Company → … → observable outcome

### Preconditions
Environment, auth, migrations, seed identities

### Steps
1. …
2. …

### Expected business outcomes
- …

### Related domains (re-run triggers)
- …

### Last run
Date · Environment URL · Result Pass/Fail · Evidence notes
```

Template: `docs/governance/E2E-BUSINESS-SCENARIO-PACK-TEMPLATE.md`

## Claims language

| Claim | Allowed only when |
|-------|-------------------|
| Ready for Business Certification | Scenario Pack **Pass** on live app |
| Business Certified | Product Owner acceptance **after** Scenario Pass |
| OPEN | Scenario Fail, not run, or stale after related-domain change |
| Verify script Pass | Engineering gate only — never “Certified” |

